                <pb facs="0531" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.248/302: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-28T16:00:00+00:00">November 28, 1939—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2844. I communicated the substance of your No. 1443, November 25, 3 p.m., gently
                    to Daladier today. He said that he understood but could not escape from the
                    conclusion that it would be essential for me to make such a trip in the month of
                    January. I left the matter there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
